+// r36 F1 (Claude as builder while Seto is out, 5 Nov 2026; fix approved by Kevy 4 Nov 08:23 WITA; ChatGPT reviews).
+// NATIVE repro of F1: a removal intent armed by our first Widow Anchor must not be applied to a SECOND copy of the same
+// card activated later in the same chain (different chain link, different S/T instance). Real engine (s3-harness
+// scenario), turn 3 Main Phase 1. Link 1 = Widow Anchor from hand (the pilot's removal activation, real removalFor
+// intent, armed through observe()). At our next chain window the trace FORCES the Set Widow Anchor (S/T sequence 1)
+// as link 2 and answers its target prompt with a deliberate baseline (the other face-up Effect Monster offered: our Kagari); every following
+// prompt is recorded with the real pilot answer (plan() -> base() -> removalFollowUp) and its follow-up stats, plus
+// the follow-up's answer to an adversarial baseline. Expected after the fix: link 2's target and its resolution YesNo
+// are NOT touched by link 1's intent; link 1's own resolution YesNo is still verified/overridden.
+// Usage: node tools/r36-f1-native.mjs <outdir>     (dev tool; no proof seeds; one engine at a time)
+import fs from 'node:fs';
+import {engine,stopEngine,scenario,drive,labels,M,R} from './s3-harness.mjs';
